1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,200
Namaste. This is SAKSHI.

2
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:12,582
Colleges tell AICTE how many students they admitted.

3
00:00:12,682 --> 00:00:18,186
SAKSHI helps check that number, without collecting anyone's identity.

4
00:00:18,286 --> 00:00:21,300
Let us start the story.

5
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:27,620
Colleges report seats. But how does AICTE check the number?

6
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:33,540
Collecting every identity is risky; families can now say no.

7
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:36,500
So we built a witness.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,692
A college uploads its list.

9
00:00:39,792 --> 00:00:45,833
Each ID is checked once, and turned into a private seal.

10
00:00:45,933 --> 00:00:50,300
AICTE keeps the seal. The ID is forgotten.

11
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:56,055
Asha has no APAAR ID. That is her right.

12
00:00:56,155 --> 00:01:02,600
Her seat is still counted, with no flag and no penalty.

13
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:06,522
Ravi took seats in two colleges.

14
00:01:06,622 --> 00:01:12,391
AICTE sees the same seal twice, but never his name.

15
00:01:12,491 --> 00:01:16,500
So it just asks the two colleges.

16
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,616
Meera sees a college she never joined.

17
00:01:21,716 --> 00:01:25,658
She taps, "This is not me".

18
00:01:25,758 --> 00:01:29,700
AICTE gets the dispute at once.

19
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:33,757
An employer scans Ravi's QR code.

20
00:01:33,857 --> 00:01:39,243
The signature checks out, with no database of names.

21
00:01:39,343 --> 00:01:42,900
Ravi shares only what he chooses.

22
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,006
Do not trust us. Check.

23
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:51,418
One button scans the whole database for raw student IDs.

24
00:01:51,518 --> 00:01:52,500
Zero found.

25
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:57,500
Now, the live system.

26
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:01,222
This is the live system.

27
00:02:01,322 --> 00:02:12,100
Every number comes straight from the database: seats counted, seats verified, and a live scan for raw IDs.

28
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:17,275
Step one. A college uploads its admissions list.

29
00:02:17,375 --> 00:02:23,988
Watch each ID become a seal, and then the IDs are gone.

30
00:02:24,088 --> 00:02:30,700
Every row shows its seal, and whether it is verified or attested.

31
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:34,381
Step two. The duplicate radar.

32
00:02:34,481 --> 00:02:38,554
This is Ravi's seal, in two colleges.

33
00:02:38,654 --> 00:02:42,727
AICTE sends an inquiry to both colleges.

34
00:02:42,827 --> 00:02:46,900
It is written to a tamper-evident log.

35
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:55,115
Step three. Each college gets an integrity score, with the reason in points.

36
00:02:55,215 --> 00:02:56,826
No black box.

37
00:02:56,926 --> 00:03:03,100
And the season replay shows how seats filled, day by day.

38
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:06,178
Finally, the privacy proof.

39
00:03:06,278 --> 00:03:09,150
One click scans every table.

40
00:03:09,250 --> 00:03:14,500
Zero raw student IDs found. That is the proof.

41
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:18,700
SAKSHI. Verify without collecting.

42
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:24,300
A witness that confirms, and never discloses.

43
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,900
Thank you.
